    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0217" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg147"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-07-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 4, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I should feel much obliged, if you have the
                    means of doing so, if you would inform me of the exact date at which a demand,
                    similar to that made by you in the case of the Emily St. Pierre, was made by the
                    British government upon that of the United States for the restoration of a
                    vessel seized by a British cruiser, but afterwards recaptured by the crew.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
